      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we can safely use REMOTE_USER with the current Keystone code. First of all, https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/auth/controllers.py#L464 the only check is:\n\nif context[\u0027environment\u0027].get(\u0027REMOTE_USER\u0027):\n   ... continue authn with \u0027external\u0027 method.\n\n How can we then handle configuration where external and any of federation methods are used (saml2, oidc, x509) ? I think Keystone will always try to use \u0027external\u0027.\n\nA check in contrib.federation.utils.RuleProcessor: https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/master/keystone/contrib/federation/utils.py#L224 will always enforce building a Rule Mapping where a \u0027name\u0027 value created. What is a goal for overwriting user_id value with REMOTE_USER?\n\nAlso, I cannot see any unit test that properly uses federated method and sets REMOTE_USER in the environment.",
